{"kind":"request","text":"Four M1a seals compute under the existing algorithm. Whole-owner and named seals both stop on check.ts because the parser returns a native BigInt value for its existing 0n literal and JSON cannot encode it. The parser also records a canonical decimal bigint field. I propose retaining that field and encoding the redundant value as null only after checking the two agree, using the same cleaner for whole and named seals. The representation distinguishes integer literals, BigInt literals and strings; equivalent hex BigInt spelling shares a seal. Existing non-BigInt seal bytes stay identical. Add one regression control and keep runtime graph code untouched.","body":{"conditions":"Rule on the minimal shared test-tool normalization required to seal the approved package-graph owner.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}